                    <h3>What is a Mutual Fund?</h3>
                    <p>
                        A Mutual Fund collects money from many investors and invests that money in different securities such as shares, bonds, and other investments. This allows investors to participate in the market without directly selecting every individual investment.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Invest in a professionally managed portfolio.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Spread investments across different securities for diversification.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Choose from different types of Mutual Funds based on your financial goals.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Start investing through suitable investment methods such as lump-sum or systematic investments.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Mutual Funds can be used for different financial goals such as building long-term wealth, planning for children's education, preparing for retirement, or creating funds for future needs. The right choice depends on your financial goal, investment period, and ability to take market-related risk.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before investing, understand the fund's objective, risk level, investment period, charges, and other applicable terms. Mutual Fund investments are subject to market risks, and the value of investments can increase or decrease depending on market conditions.
                    </p>
